You may need to download and install openssl on your terminal.
Make sure you add it to PATH, so you can run it from your CLI.

Step 1

```
cd ~/.ssh
openssl genrsa 2048 | openssl pkcs8 -topk8 -inform PEM -out typeform_snowflake_tf_snow_key.p8 -nocrypt
openssl rsa -in typeform_snowflake_tf_snow_key.p8 -pubout -out typeform_snowflake_tf_snow_key.pub
```

Step 2

```
USE ROLE SECURITYADMIN;
CREATE USER TERRAFORM RSA_PUBLIC_KEY='RSA_PUBLIC_KEY_HERE' DEFAULT_ROLE=PUBLIC MUST_CHANGE_PASSWORD=FALSE;
```
Add the below to the above SQL replacing RSA_PUBLIC_KEY_HERE

`cat ~/.ssh/typeform_snowflake_tf_snow_key.pub | grep -v "-" | pbcopy`

Step 3

```
GRANT ROLE SYSADMIN TO USER TERRAFORM;
GRANT ROLE SECURITYADMIN TO USER TERRAFORM;
```

